# Byte-integrity policy (TASK-001-CLOSEOUT).
#
# The frozen baseline is SHA-256 locked on raw file bytes, and future
# fixtures are byte-addressed imports. Git must therefore never convert
# line endings or encodings on checkout, on any platform: what is stored
# is exactly what gets checked out and hashed.
#
# New text files are authored as LF (see .editorconfig), enforced by the
# T001 smoke guardrail which rejects CRLF in project files.
* -text
